message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below. A paper preprint is pending; cite the repository until it appears."
title: "Incentre lattice"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Arifuddin"
    given-names: "Ahraz"
    affiliation: "Aska Digital"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aska-digital/incentre-lattice"
url: "https://github.com/aska-digital/incentre-lattice"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Incentre lattice: a construction (incentres of the pyramids of a polytope, joined into a contact framework) with interactive
  explanations and replayable checks. The checked results are the n-dimensional rigidity counts and Poisson ratio of the
  contact framework of the truncated n-cubic honeycomb, a radius-ratio identity, the maximal packing fraction of the CaB6
  structure type, and a sampled bar-preserving path from the cab contact framework to hcp and fcc close packing in a 2x2x2
  supercell. Claims are labelled PROVEN (written proof), VERIFIED (finite check, not a proof) or KNOWN (cited).
  Code is MIT licensed; text and figures are CC BY 4.0. Parts were produced with AI assistance; see CONTRIBUTORS.md.
keywords:
  - rigidity theory
  - contact frameworks
  - sphere packing
  - radius ratio
  - hexaboride
  - reproducible research
